{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>and behold, you have not listened until now</b> — because this is a plague, and from now on He will begin to strike him. He told him that his wickedness brings upon him punishment for not having heeded the command of his Creator. Now, Pharaoh did not say to them explicitly that he would not listen and not send them, except the first time when he said, \"I do not know YHWH, and neither will I send Israel\" (Exodus 5:2). And he did not rebuke them; he only heard their words and remained silent, for he feared the plagues from the time they performed before him the sign of the serpent and it swallowed their staffs. But in the first plagues he tests the sorcerers to do the like, that is, to show that they are acts of sorcery. And so he is afraid but hardens himself — and this is the meaning of \"and the heart of Pharaoh was hardened\"."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:36.557853463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}